{
 "version": "3.2",
 "branch": "3.2_live",
 "_note": "Official miHoYo 3.2_live hotpatch outputs (the final in-version state of the 3.2 client: res 11611027, data 11793813, silence 11212885). Same mechanism as 1.6 and 2.8: the agent mirrors these files -- from a ready-made bundle when the manifest names one (`bundles`), then file by file from `upstreams` for whatever is still missing --, verifies them against the md5/size below, serves them token-less under /hotpatch/<path> and makes the dispatch advertise them. Payloads = every file that differs from the shipped 3.2.0 client (res_revision 11078128 / data_revision 11077560 / silence_revision 10998085): 11 res files (8 new blocks, 2 changed, the release tier's asset index under its remoteName 25704984.blk) and 18 data blocks, plus the complete silence set (29342328.blk is the one that changed), the unchanged svc_catalog and the other tiers' asset index (31049740.blk), so no client tier asks for a file the mirror does not hold. md5/size of a payload = its line in the official index files (release_res_versions_external, data_versions, the silence data_versions; the asset index of the other tiers: res_versions_external); of an index file = its line in the output's own descriptor (res_version_md5, data_version_md5, silence_data_version_md5); script_version, total_size and release_total_size by their content; AudioAssets/audio_versions and VideoAssets/video_versions = the release index's .pck and .usm / .cuepoint lines, the same bytes as the shipped client's own lists. base_revision (\"11078128 fc355ae105\") names the base output `res.base`. See docs/HOTFIX-1.6.md section 8.",
 "upstreams": [
  "https://archive.org/download/genshin-autopatch-3.2"
 ],
 "listedOnly": true,
 "_defaultNote": "defaultEnabled: a Prepare from the Server page or from Quick Start switches this hotpatch on for a stack that holds no decision yet; any value other than the boolean true reads as false.",
 "defaultEnabled": true,
 "_upstreamNote": "The official CDN holds no 3.2_live file, so `upstreams` names a public copy of the outputs in the CDN layout (archive.org item genshin-autopatch-3.2: every 3.2_live output, the base output with its voice packs included; every file below and every base voice pack equals its official index line by md5 + size); the agent appends the CDN-relative path. It is a third party's copy, hence `listedOnly`: in this branch the token-less /hotpatch/ route serves and fetches only the files listed below and the base-output voice packs the mirrored, md5-verified release index names, each proven by its official md5 + size -- no unlisted file is fetched on demand and nothing else of that copy is ever served.",
 "_bundleNote": "Ready-made bundles of the same files (CDN-relative layout inside; a voice bundle holds client_game_res/<branch>/<res.base output>/client/StandaloneWindows64/AudioAssets/<Lang>/*.pck; 7z, stored without recompression). The agent downloads a bundle first (resumable, md5 + size verified), unpacks it into a staging folder OUTSIDE the mirror and moves ONLY the files whose md5/size match this manifest (or, for voice packs, the mirrored official release index) into the mirror; whatever is still missing comes from `upstreams` file by file, which is also the whole path when a bundle cannot be used -- and, for the hotpatch files, while the manifest names no `bundles.hotpatch`. url is stored percent-encoded and used as-is; md5/size = the values of the hosting archive.org item's <item>_files.xml. GIO_HOTPATCH_BUNDLES=0 switches the bundles off.",
